{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## RCA — CORRECTED (supersedes the earlier comment; ultrathink + runtime experiments)\n\n**Observed failure:** epic REB-3233 (3d7a-7795) close ran the completion verifier ~40 min, 3/3, then\nfaulted \"completion verification workflow did not produce a verdict\" with **exit 1** (hard,\nnon-retryable, offers `--force`).\n\n**Earlier RCA framings were WRONG (recorded so they are not re-tried):**\n- *\"Missing degrade arm → fabricate a deterministic verdict\"* — rejected: that verdict is\n  `certifiable=False`; close_precheck.py:696-704 would then close the ticket WITHOUT a certified\n  signature, violating the certified-close requirement and MASKING the real defect.\n- *\"600s per-call timeout too low for a large epic (scale it up)\"* — rejected by runtime\n  experiment: in a healthy Bedrock window the epic's converse calls run **~11s each**\n  (`llm_ms 361s / 32 requests`), none near 600s, and the verify COMPLETES a `certifiable=true`\n  PASS. So 600s is ample under normal conditions; the 3/3 ~40-min faults were a **sustained\n  Bedrock-slowness window** (a transient provider availability event), not a structural >600s call.\n- *caused_by = d2ce (Bedrock-default cutover)* — WITHDRAWN: the exit-1-vs-exit-11 defect is\n  **provider-independent** (it drops the disposition for ANY retryable outage), so the Bedrock\n  cutover is not its origin.\n\n**PROVEN root cause (provider-independent, structural):** a retryable provider outage that occurs\nMID-RUN in the completion gate surfaces as a **non-retryable exit-1 hard fault instead of the\nexit-11 \"transient — retry\"** the gate posture was designed to produce.\n- `close_precheck.py:629-631` is the exit-11 consumer: `_outcome = failure.outcome_of(exc);\n  _rc = 11 if (_outcome and _outcome.retryable) else 1`.\n- The classifier DOES compute the retryable disposition and attach it to the raised\n  `LLMUnavailableError` (`run_failure.py:174 provider_err.outcome = outcome`).\n- BUT the mid-run completion outage is stringified into a `RunResult.error` at the workflow-executor\n  boundary (`executor.py` StepResult/RunResult carry `error: str`, not the exception), and\n  `raise_completion_workflow_failure` (completion_failures.py:231 / the CompletionRecoveryError\n  raises in completion_recovery.py) raises a **fresh `LLMError`/`CompletionRecoveryError` with NO\n  `.outcome`** → `outcome_of(exc)` returns `None` → `_rc = 1`.\n- **Parity proof:** the plan-review gate does NOT have this bug — `plan_review_recovery.py`\n  `_degraded_plan_review_verdict` (story authorial-hated-blackbear) does\n  `outcome = failure.outcome_of(error)` then `**failure.resolution_fields(outcome)` so a retryable\n  outage maps to exit 11. The completion gate was left on \"Shape B (raised error)\" but its mid-run\n  raise path never attaches `.outcome`.\n\n**Discriminating evidence:**\n- Healthy-window full epic verify (REBAR_LLM_TIMEOUT=1200, 1 attempt): **COMPLETED, verdict PASS,\n  certifiable=true**, 10 criteria, 32 requests, ~11s/call — disproves the \"structural >600s\" and\n  \"infra-broken\" rivals and confirms the fault was a transient slowness window.\n- Small-leaf Bedrock health probe: PASS certifiable=true in 140s — Bedrock healthy.\n- Code trace: `failure.outcome_of` (failure.py:550) reads `getattr(error,\"outcome\",None)` — it does\n  NOT re-classify; the raised error MUST carry `.outcome`, and the mid-run completion path does not.\n\n**Defect attribution (caused_by = authorial-hated-blackbear / commit 3938c7ed2d60, epic jira-reb-687):**\nthat story (\"two-scope gate posture — exit 11, disposition plumbing\") built the exit-11 CONSUMER for\nthe completion gate (`_completion_precheck` raises 11 on a retryable `.outcome`) and wired the\nPRODUCER for the plan-review/code-review \"Shape A\" degraded-verdict paths, but never wired the\ncompletion gate's mid-run \"Shape B\" raise path to ATTACH `.outcome`. Consumer added, producer\nomitted, within the one integrator story — an incomplete implementation of its own design. Class:\nplan_defect. (Secondary: `failure._map` has an httpx-timeout retryable arm but no botocore arm — a\nprovider-parity gap that determines whether a Bedrock read-timeout is retryable at first\nclassification; folded into the fix for robustness.)\n\n**Fix (mirror the blackbear plan-review pattern in the completion gate):** forward the retryable\ndisposition from the primary/recovery exception's `.outcome` onto the error raised by\n`raise_completion_workflow_failure`, so `outcome_of(exc)` returns retryable and close_precheck exits\n11 \"transient — retry\" (never uncertified-closes, never fabricates a verdict). Plus add the\nbotocore/provider-agnostic read-timeout arm to `failure._map` for parity with httpx."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787541837887253001,"uuid":"bc900acc-24fc-43db-9400-3a89c7a395e9"}